From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:06:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: v14.7: Stop only the J514S/J516S panel's
 controller on DPMS off
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DPMS off stops the panel's display controller (A472 with the
hardware-power selector), and the callbacks of that transition are
answered, only on the panel this was measured on, the J514S one (the
J516S takes the same path), which the code tells by
dcp_v14_board_nits(): an internal panel admitted to the level block of
its board record. Only the T6030 record has that block today, but a
record that gains it gets the hardware power off with it: the J516C
record does with the J516C panel brightness change, sent separately,
and the J516C panel would then be stopped as well, where it has not
been tried.

Give the board record a panel_hw_off flag, set on the T6030 record
alone, and send A472 and answer its callbacks only where it is set.
Nothing changes on the J514S/J516S, and every other panel is only
blanked and leaves those callbacks unhandled, as before. The board test
checks the flag on the T6030, J516C, J514C and J613 records. Two
lifetime cases use a record with levels but without the flag: DPMS off
and on only blank its panel and find no controller to restart, and the
five callbacks stay unhandled there while the T6030 record answers
them.

Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Samuel Carreño <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
